feat(fleet): generalize trigger sources + output sinks beyond GitHub

Personal-agent fleets that live outside any dev repo: triggers for
email/SMS/calendar/file-watch/webhooks, outputs for macOS
notifications/calendar creates/outbound email & SMS/webhooks/file
writes/PD-internal. Uniform FleetTriggerEvent + OutputPayload
contracts. ConsentGate enforces opt-in on every PII-touching dispatch
with per-sink, recipient-allowlisted grants and a JSONL audit log.

Existing GitHub/git fleet shape stays backward-compatible. New
triggers (email:, sms:, calendar:, file:, webhook:, pd:) and outputs
(notify:, calendar:, email:, sms:, webhook:, file:, pd:) are
additive. Two reference personal-agent ship specs (morning briefing,
commitment extractor) + pd-fleet-personal.example.yml +
docs/fleet/personal-agents.md essay shipped alongside.

Credentials are STUBBED where operator setup is required (email IMAP,
calendar EventKit/Google, SMS iMessage/Twilio). The TriggerSource and
OutputSink contracts are wired and unit-tested; operator wires real
creds at install time.

- lib/fleet/types.ts                shared interfaces + parsers
- lib/fleet/consent-gate.ts         default-deny PII chokepoint
- lib/fleet/triggers/*.ts           9 trigger sources + registry
- lib/fleet/outputs/*.ts            8 output sinks + registry
- fleet/ships/*.md                  2 personal-agent ship specs
- pd-fleet-personal.example.yml     starter yml for the personal fleet
- docs/fleet/personal-agents.md     vision essay
- tests/unit/fleet-personal-triggers.test.js  17 tests, all pass

All existing fleet tests still pass (13 suites, 170 tests). tsc clean.


